        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/294864?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Mark WEBGL_compressed_texture_etc as supported in Firefox desktop.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This was marked as supported for mobile only, but per <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1366725\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1366725</a> it was actually about WebGL 1 vs WebGL 2 and has been supported for both since at least Firefox 55. Locally running the relevant tests in <a href=\"https://registry.khronos.org/webgl/sdk/tests/webgl-conformance-tests.html?version=1.0.4\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://registry.khronos.org/webgl/sdk/tests/webgl-conformance-tests.html?version=1.0.4</a> works for me in both the v1 and v2 modes.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29766",
            "title": "Update Firefox WEBGL_compressed_texture_etc[1] support",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-28T12:26:15.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-28T12:25:33.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "jgraham",
                "url": "https://github.com/jgraham"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10931297?u=600cfcb4c4e709dfbc66b328147d846ee87b1e51&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Update to media lazy loading added in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4071839458\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29256\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29256/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29256\">#29256</a> to note a bug meaning this is of limited use :-(</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This also updates two of the widgets to note this was released by default from 148 (but with the bug) as looks like this was missed from <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4231524909\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29434\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29434/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29434\">#29434</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">See: <a href=\"https://issues.chromium.org/issues/514611050\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://issues.chromium.org/issues/514611050</a></p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29764",
            "title": "Update lazy loading media support to note Chrome bug",
