        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 148 adds support for name-only container queries; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5184267522015232\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5184267522015232</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">@container</code> BCD file already has a data point about name-only container queries, but I thought it would be a good idea to add data points about this to the <code class=\"notranslate\">container-name</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">container-type</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">container</code> property BCD. Those pages will include examples/information about name-only queries, and I think they are common places where people will want this compat info.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29762",
            "title": "Add data points about name-only container queries",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-27T16:48:52.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-27T16:48:14.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1152698?u=5ce323090a48b425ec70128365c96809699959f7&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/iR6R7-nQeHI/m/419QMzI_AQAJ\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/iR6R7-nQeHI/m/419QMzI_AQAJ</a><br>\nThe Edge team still has the LanguageModel API behind a flag. We did not enable it by default like Chrome.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The 138 version and flag come from <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/web-platform/prompt-api#enable-the-prompt-api\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/web-platform/prompt-api#enable-the-prompt-api</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">You can test the API at <a href=\"https://microsoftedge.github.io/Demos/built-in-ai/playgrounds/prompt-api/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://microsoftedge.github.io/Demos/built-in-ai/playgrounds/prompt-api/</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29751",
            "title": "Update edge support data in LanguageModel.json",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-26T14:08:37.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-26T14:03:24.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "captainbrosset",
                "url": "https://github.com/captainbrosset"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF152 adds support for the <a href=\"https://github.com/tc39/proposal-intl-locale-info\">TC39 Intl.Locale info proposal</a> in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1693576\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1693576</a>, behind the pref <code class=\"notranslate\">javascript.options.experimental.intl_locale_info</code> and <strong>only</strong> in nightly.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This updates the following features with the support information:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/Locale/getCalendars\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Intl.Locale.prototype.getCalendars()</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/Locale/getCollations\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Intl.Locale.prototype.getCollations()</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/Locale/getHourCycles\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Intl.Locale.prototype.getHourCycles()</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/Locale/getNumberingSystems\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Intl.Locale.prototype.getNumberingSystems()</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/Locale/getTextInfo\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Intl.Locale.prototype.getTextInfo()</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/Locale/getTimeZones\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Intl.Locale.prototype.getTimeZones()</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/Locale/getWeekInfo\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Intl.Locale.prototype.getWeekInfo()</code></a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4470132900\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44172\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44172/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44172\">mdn/content#44172</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29748",
            "title": "FF152 TC39 Intl.Locale info proposal",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-26T06:39:03.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-26T06:38:28.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF152 adds support for the <a href=\"https://github.com/tc39/proposal-iterator-includes\">TC39 Iterator proposal</a> in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2025779\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2025779</a> behind pref <code class=\"notranslate\">javascript.options.experimental.iterator_includes</code></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds the feature for the <code class=\"notranslate\">Iterator.includes()</code> builtin.<br>\nNote, I can't see evidence it is supported yet by anyone other than FF, which seems reasonable given it is early in the cycle.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It fails because of the spec url which is the github repo.<br>\nI tried <a href=\"https://tc39.es/proposal-iterator-includes/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://tc39.es/proposal-iterator-includes/</a> as well but that didn't work.<br>\nI'm after advice, since it looks in the browser spec repo that tc39 specs are allowed ....</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4469264809\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44158\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44158/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44158\">mdn/content#44158</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29746",
            "title": "FF152 TC39 Iterator includes",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-26T05:59:45.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-26T05:04:54.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF152 adds support for importing text modules in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2024854\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2024854</a> (this uses the <code class=\"notranslate\">with</code> clause <code class=\"notranslate\">{type: \"text\"}</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds the text type subfeature, and corresponding <code class=\"notranslate\">text</code> destination for fetch requests. This doesn't seem to be supported in Chrome or Safari (quick search). I've set other platforms to false, except for BUN</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4470056163\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44166\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44166/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44166\">mdn/content#44166</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29745",
            "title": "FF152 with clause {type: \"text\"}",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-31T23:38:37.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-26T02:57:17.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35173023?u=c32269fffe4bd6451bfd635c7fb7d42185edf93c&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds to the data that Node 26.0.0 supports <code class=\"notranslate\">[Weak]Map.getOrInsert[Computed]</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">Iterator.concat</code></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Running the following code in Node.js 26.0.0 outputs the expected results:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"console.log(new Map().getOrInsert(&quot;key&quot;, &quot;val&quot;));\nconsole.log(Array.from(Iterator.concat([1], [2])));\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">console</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">log</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-k\">new</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">Map</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">getOrInsert</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s\">\"key\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-s\">\"val\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">console</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">log</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-v\">Array</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">from</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-v\">Iterator</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">concat</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">[</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">1</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">]</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">[</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">2</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">]</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is noted in the <a href=\"https://github.com/nodejs/node/releases/tag/v26.0.0\">Node.js 26.0.0 Changelog</a> under the \"V8 14.6\" section.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29742",
            "title": "Node.js 26.0.0 Upsert and Iterator sequencing",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-25T10:43:14.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-25T10:42:40.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ginnyTheCat",
                "url": "https://github.com/ginnyTheCat"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 150 adds support for the <a href=\"https://webaudio.github.io/web-speech-api/#dom-speechrecognitionoptions-quality\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">SpeechRecognitionOptions</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">quality</code> property</a>. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136859632107520\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5136859632107520</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a data point for the <code class=\"notranslate\">options</code> object overall, and then a subdata point for <code class=\"notranslate\">quality</code>, for both methods that use this <code class=\"notranslate\">options</code> object — <code class=\"notranslate\">available()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">install()</code>. I am not 100% sure about this structure, but I copied it from </p><div class=\"Box Box--condensed my-2\">\n  <div class=\"Box-header f6\">\n    <p class=\"mb-0 text-bold\">\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/blob/c0772004be4201be3fd9e0de1099998bc0654e9c/javascript/builtins/Intl/NumberFormat.json#L229\">browser-compat-data/javascript/builtins/Intl/NumberFormat.json</a>\n    </p>\n    <p class=\"mb-0 color-fg-muted\">\n         Line 229\n      in\n      <a data-pjax=\"true\" class=\"commit-tease-sha Link--inTextBlock\" href=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/commit/c0772004be4201be3fd9e0de1099998bc0654e9c\">c077200</a>\n    </p>\n  </div>\n  <div itemprop=\"text\" class=\"Box-body p-0 blob-wrapper blob-wrapper-embedded data\">\n    <table class=\"highlight tab-size mb-0 js-file-line-container\" data-tab-size=\"8\" data-paste-markdown-skip=\"\">\n\n        <tbody><tr class=\"border-0\">\n          <td id=\"L229\" class=\"blob-num border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default\" data-line-number=\"229\"></td>\n          <td id=\"LC229\" class=\"blob-code border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default blob-code-inner js-file-line\"> <span class=\"pl-ent\">\"options_parameter\"</span>: { </td>\n        </tr>\n    </tbody></table>\n  </div>\n</div>\n.<p></p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29741",
            "title": "Add data for SpeechRecognition quality option",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-29T08:21:14.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-25T09:38:21.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF152 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">configuration.type.webrtc</code> option to be passed to <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/MediaCapabilities/decodingInfo#webrtc\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MediaCapabilities.decodingInfo()</code></a> and <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/MediaCapabilities/encodingInfo#webrtc\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MediaCapabilities.encodingInfo()</code></a> , and removes the non-standard \"alias\" <code class=\"notranslate\">transmission</code> that has been around since FF63ish. The addition is behind the flag <code class=\"notranslate\">media.mediacapabilities.webrtc.enabled</code>. Bug is <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1825286\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1825286</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To do this I have created a structure of nested features to mirror the <code class=\"notranslate\">configuration</code> option, which has <code class=\"notranslate\">type</code> property, and below that has the new <code class=\"notranslate\">webrtc</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">transmission</code> (to be removed when this is merged). Also moved an existing key below that configuraiton option.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4470137827\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44174\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/44174/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44174\">mdn/content#44174</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29739",
            "title": "FF152 MediaCapabilities.decodingInfo/encodingInfo() - config.type.webrtc option",
            "date_modified": "2026-05-25T23:36:58.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-05-25T06:38:44.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Add details of Chrome support for <code class=\"notranslate\">\"tab\"</code> in <code class=\"notranslate\">contextMenus</code> (which is offered on Firefox through the <code class=\"notranslate\">menus</code>API.)</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #29704.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4476796340\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29704\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29704/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29704\">#29704</a></p>",
